Laut Hideung.
On average, the Turkish commercial fishing fleet catches around 300,000 tons per yéar, mainly in winter. The largest catch is in November and December.
<h3>Péru</h3>
Péru.
The &lt;a href="Peruvian%20anchovy"&gt;Peruvian anchovy&lt;/a&gt; fishery is &lt;a href="List%20of%20commercially%20important%20fish%20species"&gt;one of the largest in the world&lt;/a&gt;, far exceeding catches of the other anchovy species.
In 1973 it collapsed catastrophically due to the combined effects of overfishing and &lt;a href="El%20Ni%C3%B1o"&gt;El Niño&lt;/a&gt; and did not recover fully for two decades.
<h2>Teri cué</h2>
